{title: The Ballad of the Cross}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{key: Dm}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 129}

Verse 1
By the [Dm]prophets, God foretold
of the [G]sending of His Son
Who would [Bb]give His life
to [C]set the captive [Dm]free.
Stepping [Dm]down from His throne
and the [G]glory He had known,
Jesus [Bb]came to give His [C]life for you and [Dm]me.
Though He [Dm]knew well the cost,
He was pre-[F]pared to suffer loss
and [G]give Himself as ransom for us [A]all.[A7]
Into our [Dm]hopeless world He [F]came,
Endured the [C]suffering and the [G]shame,
Every [Bb]moment staying [C]faithful to the [Dm]call.

Verse 2
Yet the [Dm]One who spoke of love
was re-[G]jected and despised;
He knew [Bb]all too well the [C]sinful heart of [Dm]men.
Those with [Dm]eyes refused to see;
Those with [G]ears refused to hear,
as they [Bb]sought a way to [C]bring Him to an [Dm]end.
By a [Dm]friend He was betrayed,
By [F]soldiers, led away,
Yet [G]for this very hour He had [A]come.[A7]
They did not [Dm]take - He freely [F]gave;
For [C]those He came to [G]save,
the [Bb]road to the [C]cross He walked a-[Dm]lone.

Chorus 1
[Bb]He could have [C]called a million [F]angels to His side,
Or [G]stepped down from the cross and walked a-[A]way.[A7]
Yet His [Dm]love held Him [F]there,
Through the [C]pain and de-[G]spair,
To [Bb]free us from the [C]debt we could not [Dm]pay.

Verse 3
In His [Dm]suffering and pain
Took the [G]guilt and the shame
As He [Bb]hung between the [C]heavens and the [Dm]ground.
Every [Dm]nail, every thorn,
Every [G]stare, every scorn
pierced the [Bb]One who so [C]freely laid it [Dm]down.
With His [Dm]face to the sky,
"It is [F]finished!" was His cry
The [G]words that broke the gates of [A]hell.[A7]
When His [Dm]final words were [F]said,
Breathed His [C]last, bowed His [G]head,
[Bb]Darkness o'er the [C]land so quickly [Dm]fell.

Chorus 2
[Bb]Yet death and [C]darkness could not [F]stand against His power:
He [G]rose, victorious o'er the [A]grave.[A7]
In His [Dm]light we now may [F]live,
By the [C]grace He came to [G]give
All who [Bb]call upon His [C]name are surely [Dm]saved![Dm/C]
All who [Bb]call upon His [C]name are surely [Dm]saved!
